  "Question": "In cyclic quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\), extend \\(BC\\) to point \\(E\\). Given \\(\\angle DCE=80^\\circ\\), find \\(\\angle A\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "80",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "An exterior angle equals its opposite interior angle, so \\(\\angle A=\\angle DCE=80^\\circ\\). (This can also be obtained from \\(\\angle BCD=100^\\circ\\) and the fact that opposite angles are supplementary.)",
